# Source of truth

`AGENTS.md` at this repo's root is the authoritative source for architecture,
naming, RBAC, and testing conventions — derived from ADR-024 and the specific
ADRs it defers to. Read it before generating or modifying any code. This file
adds Cursor-specific working behaviors only; it does not restate `AGENTS.md`.

# Working behaviors specific to this repo

- **Before creating a new class or package, check if the capability belongs
  in an existing module first.** This repo's module boundaries (§2 of
  AGENTS.md) are enforced by ArchUnit — a new file in the wrong package fails
  the build, not just a review. When unsure which of the 7 modules something
  belongs to, ask rather than guess.
- **When scaffolding a new endpoint, always generate the RBAC matrix
  implication alongside it** — state explicitly which of the 4 roles get
  access, matching the pattern of the nearest existing similar endpoint. Never
  leave this unstated for a human to fill in later (this exact gap happened
  once already this project — a new endpoint shipped with no RBAC row).
- **Never introduce a new external dependency without checking `AGENTS.md`
  §5 and the References page first** — e.g., don't add a JSON web token
  library when `aparadhkavach-commons` already has one, don't add a second
  circuit-breaker library when Resilience4j is already standard.
- **When a test needs an external dependency (Claude, Sarvam, Voyage, Neo4j,
  PgVector), default to WireMock (HTTP) or Testcontainers (DB) per AGENTS.md
  §6 — never silently fall back to a bare Mockito interface mock** for these
  specific integrations, even though Mockito is fine for everything else.
- **Flag, don't silently fix, any place where existing code contradicts
  `AGENTS.md`** (e.g., a pre-existing `_MASTER` table reference, an `/api/`
  style path). Point it out and ask whether it's a known gap or something
  new — don't assume either way.